      "classified_as": [
        {
          "id": "aat:300435416",
          "type": "Type",
          "_label": "descriptive note"
        }
      ],
      "content": "sandalwood: a scented wood obtained from several species of Santalum, also an inodorous dye-wood, used as a dye, a spice and in medicine (OED s.v. sandal n.2, sandalwood n.; MED s.v. saundre). Includes white sandalwood (Santalum album), red sandalwood / rubywood (Pterocarpus santalinus), yellow sandalwood, and the trunk or stem (stock) of the sandalwood tree."
    }
  ],
